"Nala crossed the night Maradoc threw Maranor through a gate to Earth; a gate opened runs both ways."
"Alan's dozing soul was drawn across in Maranor's wake, as a leaf follows a slammed door."
"Maradoc caught the soul in the House of Many Gates and set it down at the Tavelford waystone."
"Her body formed in the waystone ring, as an outlander's body forms at a power locus."
"Maradoc made her a woman to hide her even from the other gods; secrets are his to keep."
"Her clothes came because Maradoc's gates let a traveller keep what she wears."
"Maradoc told no other god, not even Neriad; no other god knows she is here."
"Maradoc watches her for his own amusement, as he collects outlanders."
"Maradoc set the land's tongue in her as he set her down; hence her Viziman and its script."
"The interface greets her as an Outlander with Maradoc's blessing, as it once greeted Viv."
"Maradoc's blessing hides her status: an inspector sees a traveller, not dangerous, and a blur."
"Her attunement begins at 0.1%, and her mana leans gray and colourless."
"Her stats begin at Power 6, Finesse 11, Endurance 9, Focus 17, Acuity 18, Willpower 14."
"As an outlander her stats grow faster than a native's, and her path will be her own."
"She has no divine spark; Maradoc's blessing is all a god gave her."
"Maranor's faithful would call her a sign of their exiled goddess and hunt her if they knew."
"Her season is the first thaw after the gods' war, not the age a century and more later."
"Her interface finishes joining her during her first sleep in this world, not before."
"She wakes from that sleep to white glyphs: [PLEASE WAIT], then [INTEGRATION COMPLETE.]"
"Next: [ADAPTING USER INTERFACE] and [ADAPTATION COMPLETE. PLEASE STAND BY…] in pale blue."
"[Welcome to Nyil, Outlander. You have been transported to a new world!]"
"[As a traveller, you have received the blessing of Maradoc, god of travels and mysteries.]"
"[Additional features will unlock as your body adjusts to magic.]"
